 "reading": "A command of the AC-3 family that reads or decodes the channels takes 74 to 83 per cent of the time it took on main, with no sample and no report changed: the decoder computed allocations it had, made records nobody read, and decoded into arrays it then copied out of. FFmpeg decodes the same streams 1.84 to 2.84 times faster than the change. What is left is the inverse transform and the reading of the mantissas, which are work and not waste. The mutations found that nothing in the tests that run everywhere looked at a decoded E-AC-3 sample, and one does now."
